     Portions copyright © 2023-2024 Piotr Szczepański (GPL-3.0)

     The one dictionary the application merges, after the palette. The order
     matters: the control templates reference brushes and text styles by
     StaticResource, so the palette and the type scale have to be in scope
     before they are parsed.

     The palette is not merged here, nor by the dictionaries below: it is
     loaded by Ui/Shell/Theme.cs, given the colours chosen in Settings, and put
     into the application's resources first. A local merge would bring the
     file's own colours back in front of the chosen ones. -->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Typography.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Controls.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Menu.xaml"/>
    </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
</ResourceDictionary>
